    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW264xQ1rraVxBDBip6TeNyfG)_\n\nStacked on #374 (base is its branch; it uses `sp-writing-projects`). Independent of #375, but the project groups only appear once the writing projects are known to Projectile, which #375 fixes. Retarget to `main` after #374 merges.\n\n## Changes\n- `sp-find-note` (`M-o f`) shows the notes in groups, with a heading per group like the sources in consult-omni:\n  - \"Notes\": below `sp-notes-dir`.\n  - \"Writing: NAME\": one group per Projectile project below `sp-writing-projects`.\n  - \"Writing\": below `sp-writing-projects`, but in no known project.\n  - \"Config\": below `user-emacs-directory`.\n  - \"Other\": anywhere else.\n- New `sp-note-origin` classifies a file from `projectile-known-projects` (deepest project wins, no disk lookups, cached per file).\n- `sp-note-origin-group` (`group-function`) and `sp-note-origin-sort` (`display-sort-function`) are set through `completion-category-overrides` for the `vulpea-note` category, only while `sp-find-note` runs. `sp-insert-note` and `sp-select-note` stay flat.\n- Doc `sp-org-tag-groups.org` has a new section \"Where a note lives\"; tests added to `sp-org-tag-groups-test.el`.\n\n## Not verified\n- Not run in Emacs (none in the container), so the new ERT tests were not run either.\n- Group headings assume Vertico (or Emacs 30's grouped completion list) honours `completion-category-overrides` for `group-function`.\n- `vulpea-select-candidate-path` needs a Vulpea recent enough to have it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCtkuUzuiths11Hu1j)_",
